 "description": "DC operating point of an NPN voltage-divider (four-resistor) bias network, including base-current loading.\n\nVth = Vcc*R2/(R1+R2), Rth = R1||R2, Ib = (Vth-Vbe)/(Rth+(b+1)*Re), Ic = b*Ib, Vce = Vcc - Ic*Rc - Ie*Re. Region: cutoff / active / saturation (Vce <= 0.2 V).\nArgs: vcc_v, r1_ohm (top, base-to-Vcc), r2_ohm (bottom, base-to-GND), rc_ohm, re_ohm (default 0), beta (default 100), vbe_v (default 0.7).\nReturns (structured): { ib_a, ic_a, ie_a, vb_v, ve_v, vc_v, vce_v, region }.\nExample: Vcc=12, R1=47k, R2=10k, Rc=1k, Re=220, b=100 -> Ic 4.61 mA, Vce 6.36 V, active.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
